# Initialize (or re-initialize) the localization.

# Request
# Initial pose of the base frame in the map frame. A zero stamp means "apply at the next frame".
# The orientation must be a unit quaternion; a default-constructed (all-zero) pose is rejected.
# header.frame_id must be empty or the map frame. Ignored when global_search is true.
geometry_msgs/PoseWithCovarianceStamped pose
# If true, ignore pose and search the whole map. Not implemented in this release:
# the service returns success=false and the current estimate is unchanged.
bool global_search
---
# Response
# True if the request was accepted. The core applies the reset at the next frame, and a newer
# request replaces a pending one, so this does not mean the reset has been applied yet.
# False for an invalid pose (e.g. an empty request with a zero quaternion), a wrong frame_id, or
# global_search=true ("global relocalization is not implemented"); the estimate is then unchanged.
bool success
# Human-readable result, including the reason when success is false.
string message
# Confidence of the accepted pose in [0, 1]; 0 when success is false or no score is available.
# The pose is applied at the next frame, so the result of the initial pose yaw search (init_yaw_search) is not
# known here: it is reported on ~/status (init_search, init_search_score).
float64 score
